 ground pound the top of the  tower until you've gotten 4 of the 5  shines then you'll only get 1 power up  once you get all 5 cat shines a flag  will sprout on top of the tower and you  won't be able to get any power ups  power ups are abundant so you don't  really have to worry about this but it's  nice to have the cards stacked in your  favor early on not ready to fight fury  bowser  no problem every couple of minutes fury  bowser decides to rear his ugly head  and you may not want to fight him just  yet if you've collected the necessary  amount of shines to do so  good news is you don't have to to make  fury bowser go away you can collect any  shine on the island or after a while he  just decides to leave anyways  there really isn't a downside either way  fighting and defeating fury bowser opens  more areas on the island but waiting  collecting more shines each time he  appears can deplete his health to make  the battle ahead a little easier  you can't deplete his health all the way  before confronting him though so be  careful not to abuse this or he'll get  even more furious  having trouble fighting fury bowser look  for the bells you might notice during  the fury bowser fight that you no longer  have access to your item bank  and yes you can get hit and go back to  regular mario and even little mario just  giant variants of those two so what can  you do it might be hard to spot but if  you go back to any of the cat bell  locations they've now turned into bells  you can use to go back  into super saiyan cat mario form vegeta  what does a scouter say about his power  level  it's over 9000 what nine  thousand they don't always respawn  immediately but they do respawn so don't  worry if you lose the cat suit again  the bowser amiibo is actually helpful  amiibo are pretty hit or miss when it  comes to functionality within games even  if the figurines are usually cool  but surprisingly the bowser amiibo is  helpful in bowser's fury  let me break it down every island has  these steel boxes with bowser's face on  them  how do you break them fury bowser has to  blow fire on them when he's after you  and when they break it reveals a shine  inside  now without the amiibo you can approach  this one of two ways you could stand  there and wait for fury bowser to show  up or you can head straight there as the  rain starts to fall and hope you get  there in time  what the bowser amiibo does is  automatically spawn fury bowser  yes you heard that right so now you can  get to the boxes  tap the amiibo have fury bowser open the  boxes then get the shine and have fury  bowser go away  it's true that the amiibo only works  once per shine but if you summon fury  bowser get him to open the boxes and  then collect the shine that counts as  one so you can go from location to  location and do this one after another  if you wanted  no waiting for maximum efficiency  don't forget about bowser jr bowser jr  is a very set it and forget it character  if you're playing single player  you can choose to have him help a little  a lot or not at all this amounts to  bowser jr grabbing coins or hitting  enemies off to the side so he's pretty  easy to forget  but if you ever come across these little  question marks on the wall you have to  hit  r then use the gyro to send bowser jr to  paint over them  sometimes it reveals just a power up but  sometimes it's a gold pipe that leads to  a bunch of coins  admittedly coins aren't super useful in  this game get a hundred and you get  another power up and if you die then you  lose 50 coins which is similar to the  system in super mario odyssey  but hey the more power-ups the better  right sometimes 100 coins will even lead  to a superstar  they ask you how you are you just have  to say that you're fine when you're not  really fine but you just can't get into  it because they would never understand  you can actually play bowser's fury with  two players  and player two controls bowser jr so if  that's you then you could throw this tip  right out the window while making sure  your player two isn't screwing around  making your life more difficult don't  worry about dying  jumping off an earlier point i just  mentioned dying in this game is not a  big deal  there are no lives to collect and you  can die as many times as you want the  system works exactly like odyssey  you die and you lose coins you only lose  50 coins at a time so thankfully if  you're working towards a new power-up  you won't lose everything  but otherwise there's no penalty which  gives you the freedom to explore the  world and experiment with things  also don't worry about getting all the  shines before the end if you're like me  you probably want to get all the shines  before heading into the final battle but  you also might have noticed that the  game doesn't clue you into where the  remaining shines are  or how many are left fear not my fellow  completionists once you do finish the  final battle bowser jr will let you know  how many are left  and where the rest are on the map there  are also some shines that can only  become accessible once you finish the  final  fight so it's impossible to get  everything beforehand anyways that's not  to say you should only get the necessary  amount and move on there are some  benefits to having extra cat shines in  the bank  but maybe you don't save the hardest  ones for last as you progress through  the game fury bowser will show up  a little more frequently than before for  example if you have 48 shines but the  gigabyte unlocks at 50 then fury bowser  will show up even more than normal  but even if you do have extra shines  fury bowser will still show up a little  more frequently than before as the game  progresses and you unlock more islands  for this reason i recommend not saving  some of the trickier ones for last as it  can become an even bigger challenge  ones that require precise platforming  while also avoiding fury bowser's fiery  blast can be a bit of a headache  unless you're into that sort of thing  and that my friends is where the tips  come to an end bowser's fury is a  relatively short journey and i hope  these tips help you along the way  if you like this video then consider  clicking the like button and if you have  any further questions about bowser's  fury or even super mario 3d world then  feel free to drop a comment below and  i'll try to respond as best as i can  thanks so much for watching and stay  tuned to gamespot for all the latest on  super mario 3d world plus bowser's fury  [Applause]  [Music]  you
 

